{"availability":"available","full":"analogdevicesinc/libiio","name":"libiio","description":"A cross platform library for interfacing with local and remote Linux IIO devices","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":642,"forks":370,"created":"2014-02-17T13:51:34Z","updated":"2026-10-08T07:20:59Z","license":"LGPL-2.1","branch":"main","homepage":"http://analogdevicesinc.github.io/libiio/","topics":["adc","analog","analog-devices","c","dac","digital","hacktoberfest","iio","iio-devices","industrial-linux","libiio","linux","linux-iio-drivers"],"demo":"http://analogdevicesinc.github.io/libiio/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:31.153Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:31.153Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:31.153Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:31.153Z","stars":642,"forks":370}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Library for interfacing with Linux IIO devices","libiio is used to interface to the Linux Industrial Input/Output (IIO) Subsystem. The Linux IIO subsystem is intended to provide support for devices that in some sense are analog to digital or digital to analog converters (ADCs, DACs). This includes, but is not limited to ADCs, Accelerometers, Gyros, IMUs, Capacitance to Digital Converters (CDCs), Pressure Sensors, Color, Light and Proximity Sensors, Temperature Sensors, Magnetometers, DACs, DDS (Direct Digital Synthesis), PLLs (Phase Locked Loops), Variable/Programmable Gain Amplifiers (VGA, PGA), and RF transceivers. You can use libiio…","Although libiio was primarily developed by Analog Devices Inc., it is an active open source library, which many people have contributed to. The library is released under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL), version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version, this open-source license allows anyone to use the library, on any vendors processor/FPGA/SoC, which may be controlling any vendors peripheral device (ADC, DAC, etc) either locally or remotely. This includes closed or open-source, commercial or non-commercial applications (subject to the LGPL license freedoms, obligations and…"],"features":["If you want to just use libiio, we suggest using the latest release."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/analogdevicesinc/libiio/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d272ecf9c33f4306eb0acedb6a8fe6913ffd8e0076554273215c7231a41876f8","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:31.280Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:31.280Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Library for interfacing with Linux IIO devices","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/analogdevicesinc/libiio/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d272ecf9c33f4306eb0acedb6a8fe6913ffd8e0076554273215c7231a41876f8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/analogdevicesinc/libiio/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:31.280Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T07:20:59Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/analogdevicesinc/libiio/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:31.281Z","hash":"d272ecf9c33f4306eb0acedb6a8fe6913ffd8e0076554273215c7231a41876f8","originalBytes":11027,"storedBytes":11027,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["libiio","iio","license","linux","ubuntu","bindings","devices","library","macos","release","github","analog","debian","about","any","api","digital","fedora","latest","please","see","version","which","x64","branch.","bugs","build","documentation","general","open","python","sensors","source","try","v0.x","adcs","applications","arm64","ask","bookworm","bug","bullseye","closed","converters","cpp","csharp","dacs","debian12-arm","drivers","examples","feature","feedback","few","focal","fossa","found","gnu","important","includes","jammy","jellyfish","just","later","let","lgpl","main","make","many","need","old","open-source","operating","option","other","packages","provide","provides","public","pylibiio","question","questions","released","releases","stil